this is news no parent wants to hear  news no parent wants to relay  the father of jordan gatli telling  family and friends his son has died in  the war in ukraine  the 24 year old shot and killed in the  city of severo donetsk  it was something he thought about  carefully said his dad  leaving the british army in march to  join the foreign legion in ukraine  yet the situation in severo donetsk is  intense the russians concentrating much  of their firepower on the city and  ukrainian forces have struggled to hold  on  there are thousands of civilians stuck  in the city and 560 stranded in its  battered chemical plant  in a heartfelt tribute gatley's father  wrote jordan and his team were so proud  of the work they were doing and he often  told me that the missions they were  going on were dangerous but necessary he  loved his job and we are so proud of him  he truly was a hero and will forever be  in our hearts  soldiers in the british army have  praised his professionalism including  his best friend barney who joined up  with gatli on the same day in 2016.  i don't think you'd find a  better soldier than jordan in my books  to be honest with you um  he was um  unique in everything he did  his knowledge of everything was  you know  top tier i'd say he's um  my  best friend is a bit of an  understatement you know we were brothers  and the mayor of severo donetsk  alexander strook also paid his respects  we managed to reach him despite a poor  internet connection  what is your reaction to the death of  this british soldier jordan gatli  [Music]  look my reaction is this sadness and  pity which we have for every soldier  defending our city for ukrainian  soldiers for british soldiers for french  and germans anyone in the foreign legion  they defend our land and they help us  fight back  gatli becomes the second british  volunteer to lose his life in ukraine a  former commando called scott sibley died  in april he was 36  but tens of thousands of foreign  fighters remain  many joining several international  brigades after the russians invaded in  late february jordan gatli's death is  both a tragedy and a reminder of the  risks that foreign nationals take when  they fight for ukraine it's not a  skirmish it's a full-scale war and  officials have been increasingly frank  about ukrainian losses every day 100 or  more soldiers lose their lives and  another 500 suffer injuries  jordan gatli died in the desperate  defense of a region far from home  but his father said he believed in this  cause and his courage has been  recognized and praised  john sparks sky news in eastern ukraine
 

